.Dd October 29, 2026
.Dt STRINGS 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm strings
.Nd find the printable strings in a file
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl a
.Op Fl f
.Op Fl n Ar length
.Op Fl t Cm d | o | x
.Op Ar file ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
writes each run of at least four printable characters it finds in each
.Ar file ,
or in the standard input, one to a line.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl a
Look through the whole file (it always does; accepted for
compatibility).
.It Fl f
Put the file name before each string.
.It Fl n Ar length , Fl Ar length
Only strings of at least
.Ar length
characters.
.It Fl t Cm d | o | x
Put each string's offset in the file before it, in decimal, octal or
hexadecimal.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr hexdump 1 ,
.Xr size 1
.Sh HISTORY
Minkar's
.Nm
is LLVM's llvm-strings.
